<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<%- include('partials/head') %>

<body>
    <%- include('partials/nav') %>
    <main>
        <section>
            <h2>What Is a Game Engine?</h2>
            <figure>
                <img src="/img/engine.jpg" alt="Unity Engine Sample">
                <figcaption>Unity Engine Sample. Image: <a href="https://learn.g2.com/best-game-engine">G2</a>
                </figcaption>
            </figure>
            <p>Game Engines allow developers to design, animate and program the front and back end of high-quality
                games</p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Popular Engines</h2>
            <div class="card-grid">
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>Unity</h3>
                    <p>Unity is an engine best suited for both 2D and 3D development. Amateurs and Professionals use
                        Unity for its ease of access and its capabilities for larger codebases. The Unity Asset store
                        is also a draw for people so that not everything has to be made from scratch. Environments,
                        tools, and templates can start a project with ease of setup being a key feature of Unity.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>Unreal Engine</h3>
                    <p>Unreal Engine is best for high-fidelity, photorealistic 3D games. Unreal Engine is able to be
                        used by Amateurs however it is better suited for experienced users for the difficulty of
                        creating a game that runs well and has unique gameplay elements. Many Amateurs who use Unreal
                        Engine are unable to use the full potential of the Engine and the end result appears extremely
                        similar to other titles made with Unreal Engine.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>Godot</h3>
                    <p>Godot is a fully open source engine that requires no license or subscription. Godot engine is
                        also known for being easy to pickup and runs smoothly on almost any machine.
                        Many features are built into the editor natively such as scripting, animation, tilemaps, a
                        visual shade editor, and a clean UI system. This Engine is growing in popularity for more
                        Indie Studios.
                    </p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="sources">
            <h2>Sources</h2>
            <ul>
                <li><a href="https://learn.g2.com/best-game-engine">The 7 Best Game Engines of 2026: My Evaluation as a
                        Gamer</a></li>
            </ul>
        </section>
    </main>
    <%- include('partials/footer') %>
</body>

</html>
